  "sport": "floorball",
  "title": "The Staircase – two wall passes up the side and a one-timer",
  "description": "Three lines along one side: A at their own goal line, B by the boards just short of the centre and C by the boards in the other half. A goalkeeper in the far goal. A carries the ball a few steps and passes to B, who plays it straight back. A carries on with the ball, passes to C and sprints towards the slot. C plays a first-time pass and A shoots first time.\n\nRotation: A to C, C to B and B to A. Run it mirrored too, preferably both ways at once with lines on each side. The diagram is not to scale.",
  "coachingPoints": [
    {
      "id": "cp1",
      "text": "The receiver shows with the stick where the pass should go."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp2",
      "text": "Pass in front of A, so A never has to slow down."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp3",
      "text": "High tempo in the runs all the way into the slot."
    },
    {
      "id": "cp4",
      "text": "The one-timer should hit the target."
    }
  ],
